# Server-side runtime artifacts — must never be committed back to main.
# The bot runs from a git checkout on shkn.ws and commits its state
# (bans.db, logs, health) back to the repo; these lines keep the
# execution environment out of that.
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Local env files (real secrets live in /etc/csbb/csbb.env on the server
# and in GitHub Actions secrets — never in the repo).
.env
*.env
!.env.example

# Ephemeral per-run heartbeat/health state. Regenerated every run and
# changing every run, so committing it produced ~288 commits a day
# (and ~288 GitHub Pages rebuilds, whose overlapping builds
# intermittently failed on duplicate artifacts). Nothing reads the git
# copy: the internal Grafana panel reads /opt/csbb-private/sub_health.json
# on the server, and liveness is now signalled via healthchecks.io.
bot_health.json
